1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,871
It's late at a small clinic.

2
00:00:02,908 --> 00:00:06,337
The receptionist wants to go home, so they

3
00:00:06,373 --> 00:00:09,802
paste the discharge notes into an AI
chatbot.

4
00:00:09,839 --> 00:00:11,982
They didn't do anything wrong.

5
00:00:12,018 --> 00:00:15,018
But the diagnosis has left the building.

6
00:00:15,055 --> 00:00:16,769
The problem isn't people.

7
00:00:16,806 --> 00:00:20,663
Nobody gave them a safe way to use AI.

8
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:22,586
This is Chaperone.

9
00:00:22,836 --> 00:00:29,265
It runs on the office laptop and checks
every message before it reaches an AI.

10
00:00:29,515 --> 00:00:31,658
One sentence about Vikram's salary.

11
00:00:31,909 --> 00:00:34,909
HR sends it to the internal assistant.

12
00:00:35,159 --> 00:00:36,874
It goes as typed.

13
00:00:37,124 --> 00:00:40,553
Sales sends it to an outside marketing
chatbot.

14
00:00:40,803 --> 00:00:41,803
Blocked.

15
00:00:42,054 --> 00:00:43,054
Nothing leaves.

16
00:00:43,304 --> 00:00:45,447
An intern sends it outside.

17
00:00:45,698 --> 00:00:48,698
The name and the salary are hidden.

18
00:00:48,948 --> 00:00:49,948
Same words.

19
00:00:50,199 --> 00:00:51,199
Different flow.

20
00:00:51,449 --> 00:00:52,449
Different answer.

21
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:55,014
Hiding names isn't enough.

22
00:00:55,622 --> 00:00:58,194
This Hinglish note never says diabetes.

23
00:00:58,801 --> 00:01:02,230
Chaperone blurs the test result and the
drug.

24
00:01:02,838 --> 00:01:07,981
Then a local model plays attacker and
tries to guess what's hidden.

25
00:01:08,588 --> 00:01:12,017
It still guesses diabetes, from the word
HbA1c.

26
00:01:12,625 --> 00:01:17,768
So that word gets vaguer too, and the next
try finds nothing.

27
00:01:18,375 --> 00:01:22,661
Masking only names and IDs would have
given diabetes away.

28
00:01:23,269 --> 00:01:27,983
And if it's still guessable after two
rounds, nothing is sent.

29
00:01:28,591 --> 00:01:29,877
No name here.

30
00:01:30,484 --> 00:01:34,770
But our only female cardiologist at Udupi
is one person.

31
00:01:35,378 --> 00:01:40,092
So she leaves as a doctor at one of our
branches.

32
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:43,014
Back to the clinic.

33
00:01:43,276 --> 00:01:46,704
The discharge note goes to an outside AI.

34
00:01:46,965 --> 00:01:48,680
Names leave as placeholders.

35
00:01:48,941 --> 00:01:55,369
The age and the date leave vaguer, and the
exact values stay on the laptop.

36
00:01:55,631 --> 00:02:01,202
IDs the summary doesn't need, like the
wife's phone number, are left out.

37
00:02:01,463 --> 00:02:06,178
The reply gets the real names back, only
on this laptop.

38
00:02:06,439 --> 00:02:12,439
And when the AI writes an age the doctor
never gave, Chaperone flags it.

39
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:15,014
Now the owner's question.

40
00:02:15,186 --> 00:02:17,757
Where did this patient's data go?

41
00:02:17,929 --> 00:02:21,786
One search finds every request that
carried his name,

42
00:02:21,957 --> 00:02:25,386
where it went, and how it was sent.

43
00:02:25,557 --> 00:02:28,129
The log never stores the name.

44
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:32,157
Only keyed hashes: tags that can't be
turned back.

45
00:02:32,329 --> 00:02:36,186
Every line is sealed to the one before it.

46
00:02:36,357 --> 00:02:42,786
I change one line in a copy of the log, to
say nothing was sent.

47
00:02:42,957 --> 00:02:45,529
The check names the broken line.

48
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:49,300
What if the local checks go down?

49
00:02:50,257 --> 00:02:54,543
I stop the local model and send a new
message.

50
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:58,071
Nothing goes to the external AI.

51
00:02:59,029 --> 00:03:00,743
No checks, no send.

52
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:08,300
AI agents get the same checks through MCP,
the way AI agents call tools.

53
00:03:08,671 --> 00:03:12,957
Here Claude Code checks the Hinglish note
with Chaperone first.

54
00:03:13,329 --> 00:03:16,329
The agent only gets the masked text.

55
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:21,157
On our own test messages, masking only
names and

56
00:03:21,157 --> 00:03:25,014
IDs left 23 hidden facts a reader could
guess.

57
00:03:25,014 --> 00:03:26,300
Chaperone left 7.

58
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:28,871
Sensitive details sent: 2%, against 37%

59
00:03:28,871 --> 00:03:31,443
for Presidio, an open-source masking tool.

60
00:03:31,443 --> 00:03:34,443
It adds about 2 seconds a message.

61
00:03:34,443 --> 00:03:39,157
From 13 May 2027, India's data protection
law, the DPDP Act,

62
00:03:39,157 --> 00:03:43,443
keeps every office responsible for client
data it sends out.

63
00:03:43,443 --> 00:03:47,729
Chaperone gives small offices a safe way
to use AI.
